  "mathematicalProof": [
    "The saved ActualPrimaryClassOperatorCertificate is for the same original N1 family, same parameter graph, actual H, two positive square roots and literal native potentials694..696/703..705. Its actual source-only weighted target/background leaf, exact normalized homogeneous matrix/envelope identity, protected determinant/weight floor, complete moving frame and original cutoffs are retained. Its mathematical all-finite generator is independent of its selected finite materialization order.",
    "Use the current restricted N1 F/G theorem for actual C2/proximity. For each higher fixed order the proved same actual profile C-infinity on the fixed normalized compact chart and full anchoredFTC constants, exact slow chart, frozen carriers, stable normalized Volterra differentiation and protected H/square-root recurrences give finite polynomialS constants. This step never upgrades C-infinity alone into the epsilon exponent or substitutes a new all-order numerical Bnorm.",
    "The original weighted primary recurrence gives |D^I t|<=C_I S^b_I epsilon^(1/2) sqrt(zeta) delta^(-d_I) P. The original full-potential curl recurrence gives |D^I rm|<=Cprime_I S^bprime_I epsilon^(1-kappa_s) sqrt(zeta) delta^(-dprime_I) P. Complete cutoff, connection, moving-normal and pressure terms are retained; no source derivative or tail is set tozero.",
    "The current same-domain/support theorem supplies the exact fixed phases, original common-torus descent and label/copy flat joins for every fixed derivative. Each wave registry contains exactly162 original signed rows. Group equal label/harmonic contributions; there are finitely many per label with uniform constants. Thus triangle inequality preserves both source coefficient classes.",
    "The initialized mean operations are angularly independent and do not alter the primary wave. Consequentlyw is inW^(1/2), andw−w0tan is inW^(1-kappa_s). Since0<epsilon<=1 and1-kappa_s−17/25=31999/100000>0, the latter is inW^(17/25) on the same original domain. No new threshold is chosen."
  ],
